>>    massive testing.
>>
>>  - If you run into a problem with ext3/ReiserFS/XFS these should be
>>    easily and quickly addressed by the openSUSE kernel maintainers;
>>    for JFS I wouldn't know that.
>>
>> To me as a user the first might not be that strong of an argument, though 
>> when it comes to data being mainstream is usually a good idea. The last
>> two I find pretty convincing. :-)
>>
>> Gerald
